/*Q26. Write a Java program to find how many times a given character occurs in a string.
Input Format:
• First line contains a string S.
• Second line contains a character ch, whose frequency needs to be calculated in string S.
Output Format:
• Print the frequency of the character ch as an integer.
Note:
• Character comparison is case-sensitive
*/
import java.util.Scanner;
 
public class CharCount {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        String s = sc.nextLine();
        char ch = sc.nextLine().charAt(0);
        int count = 0;
        for (int i = 0; i < s.length(); i++) {
            if (s.charAt(i) == ch) count++;
        }
        System.out.println(count);
        sc.close();
    }
}
